## What Machines Should Check (automate these)

The best teams automate the structural checks so humans can focus on judgement calls.

| What | Why automate it |
|---|---|
| Auth coverage | Never ship an unauthenticated endpoint by accident |
| Test suite (no `\|\| true`) | Silenced test failures are production bugs waiting |
| Schema migrations apply cleanly | Catch drift before prod |
| Type checking | Catch interface mismatches at build time |
| Lint | Eliminate style debates from code review |

Set these up in CI so a failing check blocks the PR, not a reviewer's memory.

---

## What Only Humans Can Check

Machines catch structure. These require judgement:

- **Right abstraction?** Did I build for the problem that exists, or a hypothetical one?
- **Readable?** Will the next engineer understand why, not just what?
- **Scoped?** Is this change limited to what was asked, or does it touch things it shouldn't?
- **Reversible?** If this is wrong, can we undo it without a migration or a customer call?
- **Simpler?** Is there a smaller version that solves 90% of the problem with 20% of the code?

