## Principles

### The gate is the work
Agents can write production-ready code. What makes that safe is not the AI — it's the gate. A PR that passes this checklist from a non-engineer is safe to merge. A PR that skips it is unsafe regardless of who wrote it.

The checklist is not bureaucracy. It is the thing that lets everyone ship.

### Write it down, not down-ish
"Use your judgement" is not a standard. This file is the standard. Ambiguity in a review checklist means the bar drifts lower every PR.

### One source of truth
If the standard lives in three places (Notion, Slack, someone's head), it lives in zero places. Commit this file to the repo. That makes it reviewable, versioned, and discoverable by agents.

### Allowlists are decisions, not shortcuts
Every exception (intentionally public endpoint, intentionally skipped test, intentionally no downgrade) should be documented with a reason. Undocumented exceptions are the same as no standard.

